{"name":"Greenwich Village","hex":"#afbfbe","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Greenwich Village","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A neighborhood of New York City, New York, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Greenwich_Village"}],"entries":[{"title":"Greenwich Village","blocks":[{"text":"Greenwich Village, or simply the Village, is a neighborhood on the west side of Lower Manhattan in New York City, bounded by 14th Street to the north, Broadway to the east, Houston Street to the south, and the Hudson River to the west. Greenwich Village also contains several subsections, including the West Village west of Seventh Avenue and the Meatpacking District in the northwest corner of Greenwich Village."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Greenwich_Village_%2827483343909%29.jpg/330px-Greenwich_Village_%2827483343909%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greenwich_Village","wikidata":"Q205380"},{"title":"Greenwich Village (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Greenwich Village is a 1944 American comedy-drama musical film from Twentieth Century Fox directed by Walter Lang. It stars Carmen Miranda and Don Ameche."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Poster_-_Greenwich_Village_%281944%29.jpg/330px-Poster_-_Greenwich_Village_%281944%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greenwich_Village_(film)","wikidata":"Q5604897"},{"title":"Greenwich","blocks":[{"text":"Greenwich is an affluent area in south-east London, England, within the Royal Borough of Greenwich and the ceremonial county of Greater London, 5.5 miles (8.9 km) east-south-east of Charing Cross. It contains the UNESCO World Heritage Site of Maritime Greenwich."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/312SFEC_LONDON-20070917.JPG/330px-312SFEC_LONDON-20070917.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greenwich","wikidata":"Q179385"},{"title":"Village","blocks":[{"text":"A village is a human settlement or a residential community, larger than a hamlet but smaller than a town; some geographers describe villages as having between 500 and 2,500 inhabitants. Although villages are often located in rural areas, the term urban village is also applied to certain urban neighborhoods. Villages are normally permanent, with fixed dwellings, however, transient villages also exist. Further, the dwellings of a village are fairly close to one another, not scattered broadly over the landscape, as a dispersed settlement."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Bourton-on-the-Water_2010_PD_09.JPG/330px-Bourton-on-the-Water_2010_PD_09.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Village","wikidata":"Q532"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/453-461_Sixth_Avenue.jpg/500px-453-461_Sixth_Avenue.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/453-461_Sixth_Avenue.jpg/1280px-453-461_Sixth_Avenue.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/453-461_Sixth_Avenue.jpg/500px-453-461_Sixth_Avenue.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A453-461_Sixth_Avenue.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Macdougal_Street_and_Minetta_Lane_street_scene_NYC.jpg/500px-Macdougal_Street_and_Minetta_Lane_street_scene_NYC.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wik